x86_64-windows  a static local in cxx1's own spelling (`f.n`, `.guard`) where clang writes `_ZZ`/`_ZGVZ` or `?n@?1??f@@` and `?$TSS` - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file", as static-local-dynamic-init.nonames records (classed by r6d, 2026-11-15).
arm64-darwin  a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`"); and a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 9 names, e.g. <__Unwind_Resume <__Z6interni.base (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
x86_64-linux  a static local named by its function's symbol and its own, `f.n`, where clang writes _ZZ/_ZGVZ or ?$TSS (docs/CLAUDE-history.md, "A function-local static is named `f.n`, where Itanium writes `_ZZ1fvE1n`"); and a runtime call or record each compiler chooses (landing pads, guard aborts, __chkstk, atexit, a throw clang keeps where cxx1 calls terminate): emission, not spelling (tests/open/names-register.txt, "Emission, not names") - 9 names, e.g. <_Unwind_Resume <_Z6interni.base (r6n, names.sh on the Windows box beside clang 19.1.5, 2026-11-15)
